---
import LayoutLive from '../layouts/LayoutLive.astro';
import { getHousePainterSchema, getBreadcrumbSchema } from '../utils/schema';

const housePainterSchema = getHousePainterSchema();
const breadcrumbSchema = getBreadcrumbSchema([
  { name: "Home", url: "https://www.opportunity-painting.com/" },
  { name: "RESOURCES", url: "https://www.opportunity-painting.com/privacy-policy.html" },
  { name: "Privacy Policy", url: "https://www.opportunity-painting.com/privacy-policy.html" }
]);
---

<LayoutLive
  title="Privacy Policy | Opportunity Painting & Renovation Services Inc. - Holliston, MA"
  description="How Opportunity Painting & Renovation Services Inc. collects, uses and protects personal information in Holliston, Massachusetts."
  canonical="https://www.opportunity-painting.com/privacy-policy.html"
  keywords="Kitchen renovation, Bathroom renovation, Basement finishing, Interior painting, Exterior painting, Commercial painting, Light carpentry, Kitchen cabinets refinishing, Privacy Policy"
  ogTitle="Privacy Policy | Opportunity Painting & Renovation Services Inc. - Holliston, MA"
  ogDescription="How Opportunity Painting & Renovation Services Inc. collects, uses and protects personal information in Holliston, Massachusetts."
  ogUrl="https://www.opportunity-painting.com/privacy-policy.html"
  ogImage="https://www.opportunity-painting.com/img/carousel-3.jpg"
  chat={false}
  activePage="privacy-policy"
>
  <Fragment slot="jsonld">
    <!-- Início JSON-LD Schema -->
    <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(housePainterSchema, null, 2)} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbSchema, null, 2)} />
    <!-- Fim JSON-LD Schema -->
  </Fragment>

    <!-- Sober Document Header -->
    <div class="legal-header py-5">
        <div class="container text-center">
            <span class="legal-badge mb-2">Privacy &amp; Data Protection</span>
            <h1 class="text-white display-4 mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
            <nav aria-label="breadcrumb">
                <ol class="breadcrumb justify-content-center text-uppercase mb-0 small">
                    <li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="/" class="text-white-50">Home</a></li>
                    <li class="breadcrumb-item"><span class="text-white-50">Resources</span></li>
                    <li class="breadcrumb-item active text-primary" aria-current="page">Privacy Policy</li>
                </ol>
            </nav>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Sober Document Container -->
    <div class="container py-5">
        <div class="legal-doc-card">
            <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center flex-wrap pb-3 mb-4 border-bottom">
                <div>
                    <h2 class="h5 text-dark m-0 border-0 p-0">Opportunity Painting &amp; Renovation Services Inc.</h2>
                    <small class="text-muted">7 Franklin St, Holliston, MA 01746 &bull; (508) 215-9441</small>
                </div>
                <div class="text-end mt-2 mt-sm-0">
                    <span class="badge bg-light text-dark border px-3 py-2">Last Updated: October 2026</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="lead" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8;">
                Your privacy is important to us. It is the policy of Opportunity Painting &amp; Renovation Services Inc. to respect your privacy and protect any personal information we may collect from you across our website, <a href="/">opportunity-painting.com</a>, and any related communications or estimate requests.
            </p>

            <h2>1. Information We Collect &amp; How We Use It</h2>
            <h3>1.1 Information Collection</h3>
            <p>
                We only ask for personal information when we truly need it to provide a residential or commercial painting and remodeling service to you. We collect information by fair and lawful means, with your knowledge and explicit consent. This includes details you voluntarily submit via our estimate forms, such as your full name, telephone number, email address, service requested, and project address in Massachusetts.
            </p>

            <h3>1.2 Use of Information</h3>
            <p>
                The information we collect is strictly used to evaluate your project scope, prepare accurate cost estimates, schedule on-site walkthroughs, coordinate painting and renovation crews, and communicate with you regarding your ongoing or prospective home improvement work.
            </p>

            <h3>1.3 Data Retention &amp; Security</h3>
            <p>
                We retain collected information only for as long as necessary to provide you with your requested service or fulfill legitimate business and accounting obligations under Massachusetts regulations. What data we store, we protect within commercially acceptable means to prevent loss, theft, unauthorized access, disclosure, copying, unauthorized use, or modification.
            </p>

            <h3>1.4 Third-Party Sharing</h3>
            <p>
                We do not sell, rent, trade, or share any personally identifying information publicly or with third-party marketers. We only disclose information when required to do so by applicable state or federal law, or to trusted service partners strictly necessary to carry out permitted construction and renovation operations.
            </p>

            <h3>1.5 External Links</h3>
            <p>
                Our website may link to external sites that are not operated by us (such as manufacturer color tools or Google Maps). Please be aware that we have no control over the content and practices of these sites, and cannot accept responsibility or liability for their respective privacy policies.
            </p>

            <h2>2. Cookie Policy &amp; Web Technologies</h2>
            <h3>2.1 What Are Cookies</h3>
            <p>
                As is standard practice with professional websites, this site uses cookies—small data files downloaded to your device—to improve user experience, remember interface preferences, and analyze website traffic.
            </p>

            <h3>2.2 How We Use Cookies</h3>
            <p>
                We use cookies to understand how visitors interact with our service pages, ensure form submission security, and improve website navigation. In most cases, there are no industry standard options for disabling cookies without completely disabling the functionality and features they add to this site.
            </p>

            <h3>2.3 Managing &amp; Disabling Cookies</h3>
            <p>
                You can prevent the setting of cookies by adjusting the settings in your web browser (see your browser's Help menu for specific instructions). Please note that disabling cookies may affect the functionality of this and many other websites that you visit.
            </p>

            <h3>2.4 Analytics &amp; Third-Party Cookies</h3>
            <p>
                We may use third-party analytics services (such as Google Analytics or advertising tags) to measure visitor interactions and display relevant home renovation information. These cookies anonymously track signals such as pages visited and time spent on site, without storing unencrypted sensitive personal identifiers.
            </p>

            <h2>3. User Responsibilities &amp; Acceptable Use</h2>
            <p>
                When utilizing our website inquiry forms or interacting with our digital channels, users undertake the responsibility to make appropriate and lawful use of the services offered:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Not to engage in unlawful activities or actions contrary to good faith and public order;</li>
                <li>Not to submit false, fraudulent, or impersonated contact information through estimate request forms;</li>
                <li>Not to introduce or spread computer viruses, malware, or harmful software designed to disrupt the systems of Opportunity Painting &amp; Renovation Services Inc., its hosting infrastructure, or third parties.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>4. Your Rights &amp; Contact Information</h2>
            <p>
                You are free to refuse our request for personal information, with the understanding that we may be unable to provide you with written estimates or project consultations without basic contact information. You have the right to request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal contact records at any time.
            </p>

            <!-- Official Document Footer -->
            <div class="legal-doc-footer">
                <h4 class="h6 text-uppercase text-muted mb-2 font-monospace" style="letter-spacing: 1px;">Official Company Contact &amp; Privacy Inquiries</h4>
                <p class="mb-1"><strong>Opportunity Painting &amp; Renovation Services Inc.</strong></p>
                <p class="mb-1 text-muted">7 Franklin St, Holliston, MA 01746, USA</p>
                <p class="mb-1 text-muted">Phone: <a href="tel:+15082159441" class="text-primary font-weight-bold">(508) 215-9441</a> &bull; Email: <a href="mailto:office@opportunity-painting.com" class="text-primary">office@opportunity-painting.com</a></p>
                <p class="small text-muted mt-3 mb-0">MA CSL Licensed &bull; MA HIC Registered &bull; EPA Lead-Safe Certified &bull; Fully Insured</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</LayoutLive>
